  "evidence_classification": "weakly_contradicts",
  "interpretation": "In the TB-A02 restoration-studio transfer context, replacing the stacked emotion adjectives with one coherent emotional direction did not improve visible emotional specificity. The precise-emotional-direction condition scored 3.25 on the primary emotional_specificity dimension versus 3.50 for the adjective-stack control, a variant-minus-control delta of -0.25. Semantic compliance, aesthetic quality, and technical-defect cleanliness were unchanged at 5.00 in both conditions, and the overall mean differed by only -0.0625. The result therefore weakly contradicts the tested hypothesis in this context rather than establishing a broad advantage for adjective stacks.",
